<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kirina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1235</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Kirina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kirina was fought around 1235 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata Keita</a> and Sumanguru Kante, ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosso-empire">Sosso</a> kingdom. Sundiata won, freeing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mande-peoples">Mande peoples</a> from Sosso domination. The victory is traditionally regarded as the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Sundiata Keita defeated Sumanguru at <b>Kirina</b> around 1235, the remnant of Ghana was incorporated into the Mali Empire, its capital traditionally said to have been abandoned around 1240.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Its foundation is attributed to Sundiata Keita, a prince of the Keita clan who, around 1235, formed a coalition of Mema, Wagadou and Mandinka forces to confront Sumanguru Kanté of the Sosso kingdom at the <b>Battle of Kirina</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mali-empire">Mali Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The mansa was the supreme ruler, heir to Sundiata Keita, who defeated the Sosso king Sumanguru Kanté at the <b>Battle of Kirina</b> around 1235 and was proclaimed mansa over twelve allied Manding kingdoms.</blockquote><a href="/societies/mali-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Mali Empire</a></li><li><blockquote>Sundiata Keita returned from exile, united the Mande clans and defeated Sumanguru at <b>Kirina</b> around 1235, founding the Mali Empire.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-kangaba">Kingdom of Kangaba</a></li><li><blockquote>The Mande clans rallied behind Sundiata Keita, who defeated Sumanguru at the battle of <b>Kirina</b> around 1235.</blockquote><a href="/state/sosso-kingdom">Sosso kingdom</a></li></ul></section>
